---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE_EMAIL } from '../../../consts';

const lastUpdated = 'October 29, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Support — EchoChess"
	description="Support for EchoChess, an offline chess sparring studio for iPhone. Contact, frequently asked questions, and how to report a problem."
>
	<section style="padding-top: 4rem;">
		<div class="container">
			<div class="support-content">
				<a href="/projects/echochess" class="back-link"><span aria-hidden="true">←</span> Back to EchoChess</a>
				<h1>Support</h1>
				<p class="app-name">for <strong>EchoChess</strong></p>
				<p class="last-updated">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

				<div class="highlight-box">
					<p>
						Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE_EMAIL}`}>{SITE_EMAIL}</a> and we will get back to you.
						EchoChess is made by one small studio, so please allow a few business days.
					</p>
				</div>

				<h2>Reporting a problem</h2>
				<p>To help us reproduce it quickly, please include:</p>
				<ul>
					<li>Your iPhone model and iOS version</li>
					<li>The Scenario name, if the problem happened inside one</li>
					<li>What you expected to happen, and what happened instead</li>
					<li>A screenshot or screen recording, if you can capture one</li>
				</ul>

				<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>

				<h3>Where is my progress stored?</h3>
				<p>
					On your iPhone, and nowhere else. EchoChess has no account and no server, so your progress, star
					ratings and Pulse counts live in a local database. Deleting the app deletes them permanently, and they do
					not move to a new device.
				</p>

				<h3>Why did the pieces fade, or disappear completely?</h3>
				<p>
					That is Ghost Mode, the app's training mechanism rather than a fault. <strong>Clear</strong> shows
					every piece normally. <strong>Echo</strong> fades the pieces to a faint silhouette a few seconds
					after each move, so you have to hold the position in memory. <strong>Blind</strong> hides them
					entirely and leaves only the coordinates. You can change the level at any time.
				</p>

				<h3>What is a Pulse, and why do I only get three?</h3>
				<p>
					Pressing and holding the board reveals the pieces for as long as you hold, and costs one Pulse.
					Each Sparring Session gives you three, which is what keeps Blind a memory exercise rather than a
					looking exercise. They reset when you start the next session.
				</p>

				<h3>Does EchoChess work offline?</h3>
				<p>
					Yes, completely. The app makes no network requests at all — the engine, the scenarios and the Daily
					Endgame are all on your device. Airplane mode changes nothing.
				</p>

				<h3>Can I play a normal game from the first move?</h3>
				<p>
					No, and that is deliberate. Every session starts from a curated midgame or endgame position, so
					your time goes into calculation and board vision rather than opening theory.
				</p>

				<h3>How do I request a refund?</h3>
				<p>
					Purchases are handled entirely by Apple, so refunds go through them:
					<a href="https://support.apple.com/en-us/118223" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">request a refund from Apple</a>.
					We cannot issue or reverse a purchase ourselves.
				</p>

				<h3>How do I reset a Scenario?</h3>
				<p>
					Open the Scenario from the deck and start it again; a finished Scenario offers a retry. If you
					want to wipe everything, delete the app — that removes the local database.
				</p>

				<h2>Accessibility</h2>
				<p>
					EchoChess supports Dynamic Type, VoiceOver labels on the controls, and Reduce Motion. If something
					is hard to read, reach or hear, tell us — it counts as a bug, not a preference.
				</p>

				<h2>Privacy</h2>
				<p>
					The <a href="/projects/echochess/privacy-policy">privacy policy</a> is short because there is
					nothing to disclose: the app collects no data.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.support-content {
		max-width: 680px;
		line-height: 1.8;
	}
	h1 { margin-bottom: 0.25rem; }
	.app-name { font-size: 1.1rem; color: var(--text-secondary); margin-bottom: 0.25rem; }
	.last-updated {
		font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 0.75rem;
		color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 2rem;
	}
	h2 { margin-top: 2.25rem; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; font-size: 1.3rem; }
	h3 { margin-top: 1.6rem; margin-bottom: 0.4rem; font-size: 1.02rem; }
	p { margin-bottom: 1rem; color: var(--text-secondary); }
	ul {
		list-style: disc; padding-left: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;
	}
	li { margin-bottom: 0.5rem; color: var(--text-secondary); }
	a { color: var(--accent); }
	.highlight-box {
		background: var(--surface-2, rgba(255,255,255,0.05));
		border: 1px solid var(--border, rgba(255,255,255,0.1));
		border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
		border-radius: 8px;
		padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
		margin-bottom: 2rem;
	}
	.highlight-box p {
		margin: 0;
		color: var(--text-primary);
	}
</style>
